// #100: `publish.js restore-drill <environment> [--plan]`. A point-in-time restore (to now) of each PostgreSQL Flexible server of an `aca` environment's resource
// group into a throwaway server `<server>-drill-<yymmddhhmm>`, a shape check from `az`, a read of the data with `psql` when it is installed, and the removal of the
// throwaway server, always. The plugin's own file: the pipeline script (agile-deploy.js) shares its helpers and never calls this.
// The source server, its firewall, its tags and the apps are only read. The Entra token of the data read goes to the child process in PGPASSWORD and nowhere else.
// AGILE_DRILL_WAIT_MS caps the restore and the wait for Ready (default 60 min); AGILE_PSQL_FAKE stands for psql in a check (a node script; `none` is no psql);
